          "why": "Hardware is defined by being a physical component, not by whether it is outside or inside the case.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Define hardware as physical computer components.\nStep 2: Identify internal physical components such as the CPU, RAM and motherboard.\nStep 3: Explain why location does not determine whether something is hardware.",
          "hint": "Consider the components installed inside the computer.",
