          "why": "Free space is the portion of usable capacity not currently occupied by the reported data.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Write the total capacity: 512 GB.\nStep 2: Write the occupied capacity: 387 GB.\nStep 3: Calculate 512 − 387.",
          "hint": "Subtract occupied space from total usable capacity.",
          "subject": "computer",
          "chapter": "operating_systems",
          "topic": "Storage Management",
          "conceptId": "computer_operating_systems_storage_management",
          "skillId": "computer_operating_systems",
