      "notes": "\n<h2>Modem</h2>\n\n<p>A <b>modem</b> is a device used to adapt data signals for transmission over a particular communication link and recover the data at the receiving end. The name comes from <b>modulator-demodulator</b>.</p>\n\n<h3>1. Modulation and demodulation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Modulation:</b> Changes a carrier signal according to the information being transmitted.</li>\n<li><b>Demodulation:</b> Recovers the transmitted information from the received signal.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Modern modems may use complex digital signal-processing techniques. The precise method depends on the access technology, such as cable, DSL or cellular communication.</p>\n\n<h3>2. Types of modem</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>DSL modem:</b> Provides internet access over a compatible telephone-line service.</li>\n<li><b>Cable modem:</b> Uses a cable television network designed to carry internet data.</li>\n<li><b>Cellular modem:</b> Uses a mobile network, such as 4G or 5G, to exchange data.</li>\n<li><b>Satellite modem:</b> Communicates through a compatible satellite internet system.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>3. What a modem does</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Connects to a compatible communication service.</li>\n<li>Adapts outgoing data to the signalling method used by that service.</li>\n<li>Receives signals from the communication link.</li>\n<li>Processes the incoming signals to recover data.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>4. Modem compared with a router</h3>\n<p>A modem provides the interface to a particular access link or service. A router forwards packets between IP networks. A home device may combine modem, router, Wi-Fi access point and other functions in one unit, but these functions are not identical.</p>\n\n<h3>Worked example</h3>\n<p>A home receives internet service through a DSL line.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The DSL modem communicates over the telephone-line access service.</li>\n<li>It adapts and recovers signals according to the DSL technology.</li>\n<li>A router forwards the home's IP traffic between the local network and the internet connection.</li>\n<li>Computers connect through Ethernet or Wi-Fi, depending on the equipment.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Common mistakes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Assuming a modem and a router always perform the same function.</li>\n<li>Assuming every modem uses a telephone line.</li>\n<li>Assuming owning a modem guarantees internet access without a compatible service and correct configuration.</li>\n</ul>\n",
