      "notes": "\n<h2>Basic Network Security</h2>\nNetwork security protects networked devices, communications, and data from unauthorized access, misuse, damage, or disruption.\n\nCommon security measures include:\n- Authentication: checking a user's identity before granting access.\n- Access control: limiting what an authenticated user or device is allowed to do.\n- Encryption: making information unreadable to parties without the required key.\n- Firewalls: filtering network traffic according to configured rules.\n- Software updates: correcting known vulnerabilities.\n- Secure Wi-Fi: using modern encryption and a strong network password.\n\nUsers should avoid sharing passwords, opening suspicious attachments, and connecting to untrusted networks without appropriate protection. Organizations should apply suitable access permissions and maintain backups of important data.\n\nNo single measure guarantees complete security. Effective protection combines technical controls, responsible user behaviour, and regular maintenance.\n",
